From 61996db868dc3bafbbb947e05624df1e97096b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:56:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 134/145] media: meson: vdec: hevc: zero the POC MSB of a
 stream-opening CRA

Seeking into a stream whose random-access points are CRA pictures ends
playback.  The first slice after the seek reports a POC of -37, every
reference lookup for the GOP misses ("Couldn't find ref. frame
4294967259"), and the firmware then stalls on the garbage it is asked
to decode - 31 in-place recoveries in a row, ending in "No dst buffer
available" and an aborted session.  A stream with IDR random-access
points seeks in both directions without a single driver message.

-37 is 219 - 256: a CRA carrying POClsb 219, with
log2_max_pic_order_cnt_lsb_minus4 = 4, run through the MSB wrap rule
against a prev_tid0_poc of 0.  The rule does not apply here.  H.265
8.3.1 gives an IRAP picture with NoRaslOutputFlag equal to 1 a
PicOrderCntMsb of 0, and that is exactly what the picture the demuxer
hands over after a seek is: the decoder has no state before it.  BLA is
already exempt because NoRaslOutputFlag is always 1 there; a CRA needs
the same treatment whenever it is the first IRAP the session sees,
which is what seen_irap tracks - it is still clear at this point,
process_segment() sets it from the same slice moments later.

Playing from the start works because a CRA's POClsb is small enough
there for the wrap rule to be a no-op, so this only ever appears after
a seek.

Fixes: a2494e69efa4 ("media: meson: vdec: HEVC decode on G12A/G12B (8-bit and 10-bit)")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
index e5cdc46e212a..8e8f72354170 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -1677,9 +1677,20 @@ static void codec_hevc_update_pocs(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	else
 		poc_msb = prev_poc_msb;
 
+	/*
+	 * H.265 8.3.1: an IRAP picture with NoRaslOutputFlag equal to 1 has
+	 * PicOrderCntMsb 0.  That is every BLA, and a CRA that opens the
+	 * stream the decoder is looking at - which after a seek is the
+	 * picture the demuxer delivered first.  prev_tid0_poc is 0 there,
+	 * so without this the wrap rule above reads a CRA's POClsb as a
+	 * counter that has wrapped and subtracts max_poc_lsb from it,
+	 * putting the whole GOP at a negative POC that no reference lookup
+	 * can match.
+	 */
 	if (nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_BLA   ||
 	    nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_BLANT ||
-	    nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_BLA_N_LP)
+	    nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_BLA_N_LP ||
+	    (nal_unit_type == NAL_UNIT_CODED_SLICE_CRA && !hevc->seen_irap))
 		poc_msb = 0;
 
 	hevc->curr_poc = (poc_msb + poc_lsb);
-- 
